# chorus golden vector: session refused (a changed key), protocol v2 message type 0x23.
#
# Committed, and never written by a test. Any implementation of chorus protocol v2 must
# produce these exact bytes from the canonical input in session_refused_key_changed.fields, and recover
# exactly those fields from them (docs/protocol.md, "Version 2").
#
# Format: whitespace separated hex bytes, '#' starts a comment.

# frame header: type 0x23, payload length 129 (0x0081), big-endian
23 00 81

# reason = 2 (key_changed)
02

# detail: length 126, then UTF-8: the endpoint id, the offered key's fingerprint, the pinned key's
00 7E 63 68 6F 72 75 73 2D 65 6E 64 70 6F 69 6E
74 2D 74 65 73 74 20 70 72 65 73 65 6E 74 65 64
20 6B 65 79 20 34 65 64 66 3A 36 37 35 61 3A 34
30 35 39 3A 34 31 65 61 20 62 75 74 20 6B 65 79
20 31 61 65 62 3A 34 34 63 34 3A 66 30 66 35 3A
63 32 30 63 20 68 61 73 20 62 65 65 6E 20 70 69
6E 6E 65 64 20 73 69 6E 63 65 20 69 74 73 20 61
64 6F 70 74 69 6F 6E 3B 20 72 65 66 75 73 65 64
